<title>JAPAN: BOJ governor to hold briefing on BOJ law revision.</title>
<headline>BOJ governor to hold briefing on BOJ law revision.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Japan Governor Yasuo Matsushita will hold a news conference at 6 p.m. (0900 GMT) on Tuesday after an advisory panel to Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto issues a report on the revision of a law governing the central bank, the BOJ said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The special study group is expected to disclose proposals for the revision of the 54-year-old law, allowing the central bank to break free from the control of the powerful Finance Ministry.</p>
</text>
